{"code":"51-6011.00","title":"Laundry and Dry-Cleaning Workers","description":"Operate or tend washing or dry-cleaning machines to wash or dry-clean industrial or household articles, such as cloth garments, suede, leather, furs, blankets, draperies, linens, rugs, and carpets. Includes spotters and dyers of these articles.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":6.38,"share":0.5535},"I":{"score":1,"share":0},"A":{"score":1.18,"share":0.0185},"S":{"score":1.36,"share":0.037},"E":{"score":1.54,"share":0.0556},"C":{"score":4.26,"share":0.3354}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":12125,"text":"Operate extractors and driers, or direct their operation.","core":true,"importance":4.44,"relevance":82.14,"frequency":5.87},{"id":12124,"text":"Remove items from washers or dry-cleaning machines, or direct other workers to do so.","core":true,"importance":4.37,"relevance":99.6,"frequency":6.01},{"id":12121,"text":"Load articles into washers or dry-cleaning machines, or direct other workers to perform loading.","core":true,"importance":4.35,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.99},{"id":12119,"text":"Sort and count articles removed from dryers, and fold, wrap, or hang them.","core":true,"importance":4.32,"relevance":93.91,"frequency":5.95},{"id":12118,"text":"Start washers, dry cleaners, driers, or extractors, and turn valves or levers to regulate machine processes and the volume of soap, detergent, water, bleach, starch, and other additives.","core":true,"importance":4.21,"relevance":89.3,"frequency":5.98},{"id":12120,"text":"Examine and sort into lots articles to be cleaned, according to color, fabric, dirt content, and cleaning technique required.","core":true,"importance":3.88,"relevance":96.5,"frequency":5.86},{"id":12139,"text":"Apply chemicals to neutralize the effects of solvents.","core":false,"importance":3.82,"relevance":53.53,"frequency":5.42},{"id":12123,"text":"Clean machine filters, and lubricate equipment.","core":true,"importance":3.71,"relevance":67.26,"frequency":5.16},{"id":12117,"text":"Receive and mark articles for laundry or dry cleaning with identifying code numbers or names, using hand or machine markers.","core":false,"importance":3.63,"relevance":51.25,"frequency":4.83},{"id":12127,"text":"Determine spotting procedures and proper solvents, based on fabric and stain types.","core":true,"importance":3.62,"relevance":77.39,"frequency":4.89},{"id":12135,"text":"Sprinkle chemical solvents over stains, and pat areas with brushes or sponges to remove stains.","core":true,"importance":3.58,"relevance":79.85,"frequency":4.83},{"id":12126,"text":"Inspect soiled articles to determine sources of stains, to locate color imperfections, and to identify items requiring special treatment.","core":true,"importance":3.57,"relevance":74.21,"frequency":5.01},{"id":12136,"text":"Apply bleaching powders to spots and spray them with steam to remove stains from fabrics that do not respond to other cleaning solvents.","core":false,"importance":3.4,"relevance":50.65,"frequency":4.85},{"id":12133,"text":"Operate machines that comb, dry and polish furs, clean, sterilize and fluff feathers and blankets, or roll and package towels.","core":false,"importance":3.25,"relevance":25.52,"frequency":4.49},{"id":12131,"text":"Pre-soak, sterilize, scrub, spot-clean, and dry contaminated or stained articles, using neutralizer solutions and portable machines.","core":false,"importance":3.24,"relevance":62.58,"frequency":4.61},{"id":12122,"text":"Mix and add detergents, dyes, bleaches, starches, and other solutions and chemicals to clean, color, dry, or stiffen articles.","core":false,"importance":3.13,"relevance":51.72,"frequency":null},{"id":12144,"text":"Wash, dry-clean, or glaze delicate articles or fur garment linings by hand, using mild detergents or dry cleaning solutions.","core":false,"importance":3.12,"relevance":35.13,"frequency":4.69},{"id":12138,"text":"Match sample colors, applying knowledge of bleaching agent and dye properties, and types, construction, conditions, and colors of articles.","core":false,"importance":3.04,"relevance":39.54,"frequency":4.36},{"id":12129,"text":"Operate dry-cleaning machines to clean soiled articles.","core":false,"importance":3.01,"relevance":35.91,"frequency":4.73},{"id":12142,"text":"Iron or press articles, fabrics, and furs, using hand irons or pressing machines.","core":false,"importance":2.96,"relevance":53.4,"frequency":4.39},{"id":12143,"text":"Hang curtains, drapes, blankets, pants, and other garments on stretch frames to dry.","core":false,"importance":2.95,"relevance":55.98,"frequency":4.58},{"id":12128,"text":"Spray steam, water, or air over spots to flush out chemicals, dry material, raise naps, or brighten colors.","core":false,"importance":2.81,"relevance":32.64,"frequency":null},{"id":12146,"text":"Mend and sew articles, using hand stitching, adhesive patches, or sewing machines.","core":false,"importance":2.74,"relevance":36.25,"frequency":3.81},{"id":12141,"text":"Dye articles to change or restore their colors, using knowledge of textile compositions and the properties and effects of bleaches and dyes.","core":false,"importance":2.71,"relevance":27.91,"frequency":null},{"id":12130,"text":"Test fabrics in inconspicuous places to determine whether solvents will damage dyes or fabrics.","core":false,"importance":2.68,"relevance":48.28,"frequency":3.14},{"id":12137,"text":"Mix bleaching agents with hot water in vats, and soak material until it is bleached.","core":false,"importance":2.67,"relevance":37.72,"frequency":4.37},{"id":12148,"text":"Clean fabrics, using vacuums or air hoses.","core":false,"importance":2.66,"relevance":35.63,"frequency":3.43},{"id":12132,"text":"Start pumps to operate distilling systems that drain and reclaim dry cleaning solvents.","core":false,"importance":2.46,"relevance":26.93,"frequency":null},{"id":12145,"text":"Rinse articles in water and acetic acid solutions to remove excess dye and to fix colors.","core":false,"importance":2.41,"relev